/// M08 CORE-047 "websocket: roots green, thirteen assert roots".
/// Source: tests/integration/websocket_test.go symbol
/// TestCurrentBundledWebSocket (L17-203).
/// Related fixture: compiler/testdata/current/ws/socket.can (read at
/// L46, staged as src/main.can at L50); every count pin below grounds an
/// assert arm in that fixture (halt 1, pump 1, socket 1, table 1,
/// boot 1, serve 1, link 1, push 1, push_raw 1, drain 1, bye 1,
/// release 1, main 1; total 13).
/// Disposition: RETAIN (migrate row; the old Go harness stays until the
/// integrator retires it after every linked row, variant, environment and
/// control has accepted evidence).
/// Protects (this file): canlc assert green with a passed report carrying
/// exactly 13 roots, grounded per function in the socket.can fixture,
/// with supplied-completion and real-can evidence present.
/// The live lifecycle, socket generation and strict emission live in
/// core-047-websocket-semantics.can; the production process shape lives in
/// core-047-run-shape.can.
/// Variants: none in this file (default only); lifecycle variants
/// (text hi, bytes [1,2,3], close 1000 done, empty drain)
/// live in the websocket-semantics file.
/// Environment: CAN_BUN_ARCHIVE + macOS sandbox-exec; requires
/// can-bun-archive, macos-sandbox-exec. CAN_TSC gates the optional strict
/// tsc leg (pinned in the websocket-semantics file). Logical gates
/// SUITE/WORK/PROC and C/R/N/S/A identities bind at P23; no live run now.
/// Descriptor timeout 120000ms mirrors the Go 2-minute ctx (L24).
/// Delegated oracles: none.
/// Execution credit: NOT claimed (accept_after P23/QHTTP/QWS unmet).
/// Case ws/ws-roots checks: assert-green, report-passed,
/// root-count, fixture-name, supplied-evidence, real-evidence,
/// halt-roots, pump-roots, socket-roots, table-roots, boot-roots,
/// serve-roots, link-roots, push-roots, push-raw-roots, drain-roots,
/// bye-roots, release-roots, main-roots.
/// Facet map (websocket_test.go legs): assert-green pins the assert
/// leg (L70-73: status 0 and empty diagnostics or the test fatals);
/// report-passed pins the report leg (L75: passed true); root-count pins
/// the thirteen roots (L75: len assertions is 13); fixture-name grounds
/// the pins in the staged fixture (L46: socket.can; L50: src/main.can);
/// supplied-evidence pins supplied completion evidence (L78:
/// supplied-completion; fixture L168-169: push stands in via
/// when-sample, L196-197: drain stands in via when-sample);
/// real-evidence pins real native evidence (L78: real-can; fixture
/// L178-180: push_raw sample runs the real bytes::from_ints on
/// [1,2,3]; fixture L93-95: table sample runs the real
/// http::route_get and http::make_router natives); halt-roots pins halt
/// (fixture L12-13: hello, 1 root); pump-roots pins pump (fixture
/// L34-35: hello, 1); socket-roots pins socket (fixture L78-79:
/// refused, 1); table-roots pins table (fixture L91-92: sample, 1);
/// boot-roots pins boot (fixture L104-105: sample 0, 1); serve-roots
/// pins serve (fixture L121-122: sample 0, 1); link-roots pins link
/// (fixture L149-150: dark, 1); push-roots pins push (fixture L165-166:
/// sample hi, 1); push-raw-roots pins push_raw (fixture L178-179:
/// sample [1,2,3], 1); drain-roots pins drain (fixture L193-194:
/// sample 1, 1); bye-roots pins bye (fixture L207-208: sample, 1);
/// release-roots pins release (fixture L219-220: sample, 1);
/// main-roots pins main (fixture L230-231: sample [], 1).
/// Shared old files untouched; retirement is a later integrator decision.
